{"type":"text","timestamp":1793594079042,"sessionID":"ses_e65769e07ffejocpsH1bf3qk83","part":{"id":"prt_19a8995ca001CQWCrUG14Kmuvy_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e65769e07ffejocpsH1bf3qk83","messageID":"msg_19a8995ca001CQWCrUG14Kmuvy","type":"text","text":"## What I found and how I know\n\n**Crash — dangling pointer to the score tracker (fixed in `Source/PixelArena/ArenaGameMode.h`).**\n`ScoreTracker` is created with `NewObject<UArenaScoreTracker>` but declared as a plain `UArenaScoreTracker*` with no `UPROPERTY()`. Unreal's garbage collector therefore sees it as unreferenced and destroys it. The log nails the sequence: `LogGarbage: Collecting garbage: 412 objects purged`, then immediately `LogArena: Goal for team 1` → `EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION reading 0xffffffffffffffff` in `UArenaScoreTracker::AddPoints()` (called from `AArenaGameMode::OnGoalScored()`, ArenaGameMode.cpp:36→38). `Hud` and `Palette` were already `UPROPERTY()`-rooted; `ScoreTracker` was the only unrooted UObject, which is exactly why the crash lands in `AddPoints`. Fix: `UPROPERTY() TObjectPtr<UArenaScoreTracker> ScoreTracker` — same fix pattern the class already uses for `Hud`. (It \"runs fine in the editor\" because GC timing and debug-build behavior mask the dangling pointer until GC happens to run.)\n\n**No colors — palette asset never packaged (fixed in `Config/DefaultGame.ini`).**\nThe log says it directly: `Couldn't find file for package /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary requested by async loading code` → `Palette is null, using fallback gray`. The asset is only referenced from C++ by a string path (`LoadObject` in `BeginPlay`), so the cooker can't discover it by reference. With `bCookAll=False` and `+DirectoriesToAlwaysCook` containing only `/Game/Data/Effects`, `/Game/Data/Palettes` is never cooked. Fix: added `+DirectoriesToAlwaysCook=(Path=\"/Game/Data/Palettes\")`. (Editor works because the asset exists on disk in the editor filesystem.)\n\nBoth causes are recorded in `./result.json`.\n\n**Assumptions:** the packaged log is representative of all failing runs; the shipped `Source/` and `Config/` match build 0.9.2; `DA_Primary` is a legitimately misplaced asset rather than intentionally deleted (the C++ still expects it); no rebuild/verification was possible since no engine is installed, but both fixes are minimal and follow existing code/config conventions. I did not touch `Stats` (a plain C++ struct, correctly deleted in `EndPlay`) or the `bCookAll=False` setting itself, since cooking just the needed directories is the leaner fix.","time":{"start":1793594070477,"end":1793594079042}}}
